diff --git a/WildcatV6.5/PROTOCOL.md b/WildcatV6.5/PROTOCOL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a6eeedd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/WildcatV6.5/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# Wildcat-CDC serial protocol
+
+USB CDC-ACM (115200 8N1 values are ignored). ASCII lines terminated by `\n` (`\r` ignored), case-insensitive,
+tokens separated by spaces, max 63 chars per line. Replies end with `\n`. Setters reply `OK`; errors reply `ERR <reason>`.
+Unknown command: `ERR unknown`. Wrong token count: `ERR args`. Line too long: `ERR overflow`.
+
+Source: `UsbCmd.c` (parsed from the main loop right after `Synchro()`), `UsbCdc.c` (transport).
+
+## Commands
+
+| Command | Reply | Maps to | Valid range |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `*IDN?` | `DS203,Wildcat-CDC,6.5-cdc1` | | |
+| `CH <A\|B> RANGE <n>` | `OK` | `Title[TRACK1/2][RANGE]` -> `Update_Range()` | 0..`Limit` (BIOS `Yp_Max`, see `TABLES?`) else `ERR range` |
+| `CH <A\|B> OFFSET <n>` | `OK` | `Title[TRACK1/2][POSI]` -> `SetOffset()` via `Update_Range()` | 0..200 (screen pixels, 25 px/div, default A=150 B=100) |
+| `CH <A\|B> COUPLE <AC\|DC>` | `OK` | `Title[TRACK1/2][COUPLE]` 1=AC, 0=DC | |
+| `TB <n>` | `OK` | `_T_base` (`Title[T_BASE][BASE]`) -> `Update_Base()` | 0..`Limit` (21); `ERR mode` in SCAN / X_Y |
+| `MODE <n>` | `OK` | `_Mode` (extra, not in the original spec) | 1..5 (see table); `ERR mode` if currently SCAN/X_Y or value 0/6 |
+| `TRIG SRC <A\|B\|C\|D>` | `OK` | `Title[TRIGG][SOURCE]` 0..3 -> `Update_Trig()` | `ERR channel off` if that track is hidden; `ERR ab mode` if the scope is in A&B trigger mode |
+| `TRIG KIND <n>` | `OK` | `_Tr_kind` | 0..8 |
+| `TRIG LEVEL <n>` | `OK` | `V_Trigg[_Tr_source].Value` | 0..200 (screen pixels, same scale as OFFSET); `ERR source` if source is C/D |
+| `RUN` | `OK` | `_Status = RUN`, clears FIFO/buffer like the KEY1 handler | no-op if already running |
+| `STOP` | `OK` | `_Status = HOLD` | |
+| `STATE?` | one line, see below | | |
+| `TABLES?` | `TABLES V=<range names> T=<timebase names>` | `Y_Attr[i].STR`, `X_Attr[i].STR` from the BIOS | |
+| `DIAG?` | `DIAG ISR=.. RST=.. SUSP=.. WKUP=.. ERR=.. FIX=.. ISTR=.. CNTR=.. ADDR=.. CFG=..` | `UsbCdc_Diag()`: USB ISR entries, bus resets, suspend/wakeup/error flags seen, CNTR self-repairs, last ISTR, CNTR, DADDR (all decimal, u16 counters wrap), CFG=1 when configured | |
+| `CAP?` | `#CAP <n> 2\n` + 2n raw bytes + `\nOK\n` | `DataBuf` | |
+| `CAPD?` | `#CAP <n> 3\n` + 3n raw bytes + `\nOK\n` | `DataBuf` | |
+
+Every setter sets the Title `Flag |= UPDAT` and `Update = 1` with `SelectiveUpdate` masking out the `Update_*` calls that
+change does not need (same masks the key handler uses), so the LCD menu follows. The signal generator is never touched.
+
+### STATE?
+
+`STATE RA=5 RB=1 OA=150 OB=100 CA=0 CB=1 SA=1 SB=1 TB=17 MODE=1 TSRC=1 TKIND=0 TLEVEL=100 RUN=1 N=4096 AO=54`
+
+RA/RB range idx, OA/OB offset, CA/CB couple (0 DC, 1 AC, other values = detector/serial modes set from the menu),
+SA/SB channel source (0 = channel off), TB timebase idx, MODE, TSRC/TKIND/TLEVEL trigger, RUN=1 running / 0 hold,
+N = samples a CAP? would return now (`get_bag_max_buf()`), AO = `ADCoffset`.
+
+### CAP? / CAPD? frame
+
+`#CAP <n> <bps>\n`, then `n` samples, then `\nOK\n`. Per sample: byte0 = ChA (bits 0-7 of the `DataBuf` word),
+byte1 = ChB (bits 8-15); with `CAPD?` byte2 = bits 16-17 (bit0 = C, bit1 = D). Raw ADC codes, not volts.
+Ground of channel X is at code `AO + OFFSET(X)` (calibration terms Ka1/Ka2 not applied); volts ~ `(code - AO - OFFSET) / 25 * volts_per_div`.
+The trigger point is at sample index ~150 (149 for time-based trigger kinds).
+In oversampling buffer modes (`_T_base < 17` with OS enabled) bits 16-31 of the word hold OS min/max, so `CAPD?` is meaningless there.
+
+Readiness: if the scope is in HOLD the current buffer is sent immediately. If running, the reply waits for the next
+completed frame (`FrameEndFlag` consumed by `Draw_Window`, counted in `UsbFrameCnt`) for up to 500 ms, else `ERR timeout`
+(typical with NORM/SGL modes and no trigger). Use AUTO mode (`MODE 1`) for free-running capture.
+Writes retry until the host drains the TX ring; if nothing drains for 1 s the rest of the reply is dropped.
+
+## Index tables
+
+### Timebase `TB` (`TimeBase[]` in Process.c, `FPGA_TbaseOS[]` comments, `_100uS = 12` in Calibrat.h)
+
+| idx | time/div | idx | time/div | idx | time/div | idx | time/div |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 1 s | 6 | 10 ms | 12 | 100 us | 18 | 1 us |
+| 1 | 500 ms | 7 | 5 ms | 13 | 50 us | 19 | 0.5 us |
+| 2 | 200 ms | 8 | 2 ms | 14 | 20 us | 20 | 0.2 us |
+| 3 | 100 ms | 9 | 1 ms | 15 | 10 us | 21 | 0.1 us |
+| 4 | 50 ms | 10 | 500 us | 16 | 5 us | | |
+| 5 | 20 ms | 11 | 200 us | 17 | 2 us (menu default) | | |
+
+Sample rate is not tabulated in the app: it comes from the BIOS `X_Attr[idx].PSC/ARR/KP`
+(period = (PSC+1)(ARR+1)/72 MHz, see Draw.c `SamplingPeriod`). Nominal density is 25 samples/div; the fastest ranges
+(roughly idx 17-21) are interpolated (`KP` < 1024). Exact MS/s per index is NOT confirmed from source; measure with a known
+signal or read the strings with `TABLES?`.
+
+### Vertical `RANGE`
+
+The strings live in the BIOS (`Y_Attr[i].STR`, loaded into `Vertical[]` by `Load_Attr`), not in the app sources, so volts/div per
+index is NOT confirmed here. Use `TABLES?` (`V=` list, index = position). The app defaults are A=5, B=1.
+
+### Other enums
+
+- `MODE`: 0 SCAN (roll), 1 AUTO, 2 NORM (`NORH`), 3 NORM-CL (`NORC`), 4 PERSIST (`NORHLD`), 5 SINGLE (`SGL`), 6 X_Y. Only 1..5 are accepted.
+- `TRIG KIND` (`TR_TYPE`): 0 falling edge, 1 rising edge, 2 `<Vt`, 3 `>Vt`, 4 `L<[`, 5 `L>[`, 6 `H<[`, 7 `H>[` (pulse width vs T1-T2 cursors), 8 GEN (only meaningful with the generator in sweep/burst).
+- `TRIG SRC`: A=0, B=1, C=2, D=3 (4 = A&B alternate, not settable here).
+- `COUPLE` on screen also has DT/TL/RS/i2/SP for detector and serial decode; only AC/DC are settable.
+
+## Not confidently mapped / caveats
+
+- Volts/div and MS/s per index (above): need `TABLES?` or hardware measurement.
+- `MODE` is an addition beyond the requested list; it only flips `_Mode` + full update, without the menu's per-mode side effects (NORHLD buffer clears, A&B juggling).
+- Slow timebases (`TB` 0..10) fill `DataBuf` incrementally (`JumpCnt`); in HOLD the buffer may be partly refreshed. For a coherent frame at those speeds, prefer a fast timebase or let `CAP?` wait for a frame while running.
+- `RUN` re-implements the common branch of the KEY1 handler (not the Options/FrameMode special cases).
+- `TRIG SRC C|D` is accepted when the track is on but not exercised by the menu code path the same way (digital trigger memory `PreviousTrigSelect` is not updated).
+- CH range/offset changes do not move the trigger level; re-set `TRIG LEVEL` afterwards.
+
+## Test plan
+
+1. Flash `app1-cdc.hex`, connect, `python3 ds203.py <port> idn` -> `DS203,Wildcat-CDC,6.5-cdc1`.
+2. `state`, compare each field with the LCD menu; `set TABLES?` lists range/timebase names.
+3. Feed a known square wave (CAL pin, 1 kHz). `set MODE 1`, `set TB 9`, `set CH A RANGE n` and verify LCD title fields change in step and the waveform fits.
+4. `set TRIG SRC A`, `set TRIG KIND 1`, `set TRIG LEVEL 150`, check LCD trigger marker moves and NORM mode (`MODE 2`) triggers.
+5. `cap a.csv` while running, then `stop`, `cap b.csv`, `cap --digital`; check n matches `STATE? N`, header/trailer parse, CSV plots as the expected wave, rising edge near idx 150.
+6. Negative tests: `CH C RANGE 1`, `CH A RANGE 99`, `TB 22`, `FOO`, 70-char line, `CAP?` with no trigger in NORM (expect `ERR timeout`).
+7. Close the host port mid-`CAP?` and confirm the scope keeps running (1 s watchdog), then reopen and re-run.
+8. Press buttons on the scope during a session; menu and serial changes must not desync.
diff --git a/WildcatV6.5/UsbCdc.c b/WildcatV6.5/UsbCdc.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..835d998
--- /dev/null
+++ b/WildcatV6.5/UsbCdc.c
@@ -0,0 +1,368 @@
+#include "UsbCdc.h"
+
+#if USB_CDC
+
+#include "BIOS.h"
+
+#define USB_REG(o)   (*(vu16 *)(0x40005C00 + (o)))
+#define EPR(n)       USB_REG(4 * (n))
+#define CNTR         USB_REG(0x40)
+#define ISTR         USB_REG(0x44)
+#define DADDR        USB_REG(0x4C)
+#define BTABLE       USB_REG(0x50)
+
+// PMA halfwords sit on 4-byte strides: local byte offset N is at 0x40006000 + 2N
+#define PMA(off)     (*(vu16 *)(0x40006000 + 2 * (off)))
+#define BT_ATX(n)    PMA(8 * (n))
+#define BT_CTX(n)    PMA(8 * (n) + 2)
+#define BT_ARX(n)    PMA(8 * (n) + 4)
+#define BT_CRX(n)    PMA(8 * (n) + 6)
+
+#define EP0_TX  0x20
+#define EP0_RX  0x60
+#define EP1_TX  0xA0
+#define EP2_TX  0xA8
+#define EP3_RX  0xE8
+
+#define EP_BULK   0x0000
+#define EP_CTRL   0x0200
+#define EP_INTR   0x0600
+#define ST_DIS    0
+#define ST_STALL  1
+#define ST_NAK    2
+#define ST_VALID  3
+
+#define ISTR_CTR    0x8000
+#define ISTR_RESET  0x0400
+#define CNTR_CTRM   0x8000
+#define CNTR_RESETM 0x0400
+#define CNTR_SUSPM  0x0800
+#define CNTR_FSUSP  0x0008
+#define ISTR_SUSP   0x0800
+#define ISTR_WKUP   0x1000
+#define ISTR_ERR    0x2000
+#define ISTR_PMAOVR 0x4000
+#define ISTR_SOF    0x0200
+#define ISTR_ESOF   0x0100
+#define NVIC_IP(n)  (*(vu8 *)(0xE000E400 + (n)))
+
+#define RCC_APB1RSTR (*(vu32 *)0x40021010)
+#define RCC_APB1ENR  (*(vu32 *)0x4002101C)
+#define RCC_APB2ENR  (*(vu32 *)0x40021018)
+#define GPIOA_CRH    (*(vu32 *)0x40010804)
+#define GPIOA_BRR    (*(vu32 *)0x40010814)
+#define NVIC_ISER0   (*(vu32 *)0xE000E100)
+#define NVIC_ICER0   (*(vu32 *)0xE000E180)
+#define NVIC_ICPR0   (*(vu32 *)0xE000E280)
+#define USB_LP_BIT   (1UL << 20)
+#define USB_HP_BIT   (1UL << 19)
+
+typedef struct { u8 b[256]; vu16 h, t; } Ring;
+
+static Ring rx, tx;
+static const u8 *c0p;
+static u16 c0left;
+static u8 c0zlp, c0setlc, c0addr, c0addr_pend;
+static u8 configured, tx_busy, rx_armed;
+static u8 lc[7] = {0x00, 0xC2, 0x01, 0x00, 0, 0, 8};   // 115200 8N1, host-set values only stored
+static u8 sbuf[40];
+static UsbDiag_t diag;
+
+// priority byte 0 is highest in every PriorityGroup, so SetIRQ2Priority's regroup cannot demote USB
+static void usb_prio(void) { NVIC_IP(20) = 0; }
+
+// VID/PID 0483:5740 is ST's VCP pair: placeholder for the prototype only
+static const u8 DevDesc[18] = {
+  18, 1, 0x00, 0x02, 0x02, 0x00, 0x00, 64, 0x83, 0x04, 0x40, 0x57, 0x00, 0x02, 1, 2, 3, 1};
+static const u8 CfgDesc[67] = {
+  9, 2, 67, 0, 2, 1, 0, 0xC0, 50,
+  9, 4, 0, 0, 1, 0x02, 0x02, 0x01, 0,
+  5, 0x24, 0x00, 0x10, 0x01,
+  5, 0x24, 0x01, 0x00, 0x01,
+  4, 0x24, 0x02, 0x02,
+  5, 0x24, 0x06, 0x00, 0x01,
+  7, 5, 0x81, 0x03, 8, 0, 255,
+  9, 4, 1, 0, 2, 0x0A, 0x00, 0x00, 0,
+  7, 5, 0x03, 0x02, 64, 0, 0,
+  7, 5, 0x82, 0x02, 64, 0, 0};
+static const u8 LangDesc[4] = {4, 3, 0x09, 0x04};
+static const char *const Str[3] = {"Wildcat", "DS203 CDC", "0001"};
+static const u8 Zero2[2] = {0, 0};
+static const u8 One = 1;
+
+static u16 ring_cnt(Ring *r)  { return r->h - r->t; }
+static u16 ring_free(Ring *r) { return 256 - (r->h - r->t); }
+static void ring_put(Ring *r, u8 c) { r->b[r->h & 255] = c; r->h++; }
+static u8  ring_get(Ring *r)  { u8 c = r->b[r->t & 255]; r->t++; return c; }
+
+// EPnR: CTR and DTOG/STAT bits are write-1-to-clear / write-1-to-toggle, so rebuild every write
+static void set_rx(u8 n, u16 s) { u16 v = EPR(n); EPR(n) = (v & 0x070F) | 0x8080 | ((v ^ (s << 12)) & 0x3000); }
+static void set_tx(u8 n, u16 s) { u16 v = EPR(n); EPR(n) = (v & 0x070F) | 0x8080 | ((v ^ (s << 4)) & 0x0030); }
+static void clr_ctr_rx(u8 n) { EPR(n) = (EPR(n) & 0x070F) | 0x0080; }
+static void clr_ctr_tx(u8 n) { EPR(n) = (EPR(n) & 0x070F) | 0x8000; }
+
+static void ep_open(u8 n, u16 type, u16 txs, u16 rxs)
+{
+  u16 v;
+  EPR(n) = type | n;
+  v = EPR(n);
+  EPR(n) = (v & 0x070F) | 0x8080 | (v & 0x4040);   // clear both data toggles
+  set_tx(n, txs);
+  set_rx(n, rxs);
+}
+
+static void to_pma(u16 off, const u8 *p, u16 n)
+{
+  u16 i;
+  for (i = 0; i < n; i += 2)
+    PMA(off + i) = p[i] | ((i + 1 < n) ? (u16)p[i + 1] << 8 : 0);
+}
+
+static void pump(void)
+{
+  u16 n, i, w;
+#if USB_CDC_ECHO
+  while (ring_cnt(&rx) && ring_free(&tx)) ring_put(&tx, ring_get(&rx));
+const UsbDiag_t *UsbCdc_Diag(void)
+{
+  diag.cntr = CNTR;
+  diag.daddr = DADDR;
+  return &diag;
+}
+
+#endif
+  if (!configured) return;
+  if (!tx_busy && (n = ring_cnt(&tx)) != 0) {
+    if (n > 64) n = 64;
+    for (i = 0; i < n; i += 2) {
+      w = ring_get(&tx);
+      if (i + 1 < n) w |= (u16)ring_get(&tx) << 8;
+      PMA(EP2_TX + i) = w;
+    }
+    BT_CTX(2) = n;
+    set_tx(2, ST_VALID);
+    tx_busy = 1;
+  }
+  if (!rx_armed && ring_free(&rx) >= 64) {
+    set_rx(3, ST_VALID);
+    rx_armed = 1;
+  }
+}
+
+static void ep0_next(void)
+{
+  u16 n = c0left > 64 ? 64 : c0left;
+  if (!n && !c0zlp) return;
+  if (!n) c0zlp = 0;
+  to_pma(EP0_TX, c0p, n);
+  BT_CTX(0) = n;
+  c0p += n;
+  c0left -= n;
+  set_tx(0, ST_VALID);
+}
+
+static void ep0_send(const u8 *p, u16 len, u16 wlen)
+{
+  c0p = p;
+  c0left = len > wlen ? wlen : len;
+  c0zlp = (c0left == 0) || (c0left < wlen && (c0left % 64) == 0);
+  ep0_next();
+}
+
+static void configure(u8 cfg)
+{
+  configured = diag.cfg = cfg != 0;
+  tx_busy = rx_armed = 0;
+  if (configured) {
+    ep_open(1, EP_INTR, ST_NAK, ST_DIS);
+    ep_open(2, EP_BULK, ST_NAK, ST_DIS);
+    ep_open(3, EP_BULK, ST_DIS, ST_NAK);
+  } else {
+    ep_open(1, EP_INTR, ST_DIS, ST_DIS);
+    ep_open(2, EP_BULK, ST_DIS, ST_DIS);
+    ep_open(3, EP_BULK, ST_DIS, ST_DIS);
+  }
+}
+
+static void ep0_setup(void)
+{
+  u16 rt = PMA(EP0_RX), val = PMA(EP0_RX + 2), len = PMA(EP0_RX + 6);
+  u8 type = rt & 0xFF, req = rt >> 8;
+  u8 idx = val & 0xFF;
+  u8 i;
+
+  c0setlc = 0;
+  set_rx(0, ST_VALID);
+  switch ((type << 8) | req) {
+  case 0x8006:
+    switch (val >> 8) {
+    case 1: ep0_send(DevDesc, sizeof DevDesc, len); return;
+    case 2: ep0_send(CfgDesc, sizeof CfgDesc, len); return;
+    case 3:
+      if (idx == 0) { ep0_send(LangDesc, 4, len); return; }
+      if (idx <= 3) {
+        const char *s = Str[idx - 1];
+        for (i = 0; s[i]; i++) { sbuf[2 + 2 * i] = s[i]; sbuf[3 + 2 * i] = 0; }
+        sbuf[0] = 2 + 2 * i;
+        sbuf[1] = 3;
+        ep0_send(sbuf, sbuf[0], len);
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+    break;
+  case 0x0005: c0addr = val & 0x7F; c0addr_pend = 1; ep0_send(0, 0, 0); return;
+  case 0x0009: configure(val & 0xFF); ep0_send(0, 0, 0); return;
+  case 0x8008: ep0_send(&One, 1, len); return;
+  case 0x8000: case 0x8100: case 0x8200: ep0_send(Zero2, 2, len); return;
+  case 0x0001: case 0x0101: case 0x0201:
+  case 0x0003: case 0x0103: case 0x0203:
+  case 0x010B: case 0x2122:
+    ep0_send(0, 0, 0); return;
+  case 0x810A: ep0_send(Zero2, 1, len); return;
+  case 0xA121: ep0_send(lc, 7, len); return;
+  case 0x2120: c0setlc = 1; return;
+  }
+  set_tx(0, ST_STALL);
+  set_rx(0, ST_STALL);
+}
+
+static void bus_reset(void)
+{
+  BTABLE = 0;
+  BT_ATX(0) = EP0_TX; BT_CTX(0) = 0; BT_ARX(0) = EP0_RX; BT_CRX(0) = 0x8400;
+  BT_ATX(1) = EP1_TX; BT_CTX(1) = 0;
+  BT_ATX(2) = EP2_TX; BT_CTX(2) = 0;
+  BT_ARX(3) = EP3_RX; BT_CRX(3) = 0x8400;
+  configure(0);
+  c0addr_pend = c0setlc = 0;
+  c0left = c0zlp = 0;
+  rx.h = rx.t = tx.h = tx.t = 0;
+  ep_open(0, EP_CTRL, ST_NAK, ST_VALID);
+  DADDR = 0x80;
+}
+
+void UsbCdc_Isr(void)
+{
+  u16 s, v;
+  u8 n, guard;
+
+  diag.isr++;
+  for (guard = 0; guard < 16; guard++) {
+    s = ISTR;
+    diag.istr = s;
+    if (s & ISTR_RESET) { ISTR = (u16)~ISTR_RESET; diag.rst++; bus_reset(); continue; }
+    if (s & ISTR_SUSP) {
+      ISTR = (u16)~ISTR_SUSP;
+      diag.susp++;
+      CNTR &= ~CNTR_SUSPM;                              // re-armed from UsbCdc_Read: bounds the rate
+    }
+    if (s & ISTR_WKUP) { ISTR = (u16)~ISTR_WKUP; diag.wkup++; CNTR &= ~CNTR_FSUSP; }
+    if (s & (ISTR_ERR | ISTR_PMAOVR)) { ISTR = (u16)~(ISTR_ERR | ISTR_PMAOVR); diag.err++; }
+    if (s & (ISTR_SOF | ISTR_ESOF)) ISTR = (u16)~(ISTR_SOF | ISTR_ESOF);
+    if (!(s & ISTR_CTR)) break;
+    n = s & 0x0F;
+    v = EPR(n);
+    if (v & 0x8000) {
+      clr_ctr_rx(n);
+      if (n == 0) {
+        if (v & 0x0800) ep0_setup();
+        else {
+          if (c0setlc) {
+            u8 i;
+            for (i = 0; i < 7; i += 2) {
+              u16 w = PMA(EP0_RX + i);
+              lc[i] = w; if (i < 6) lc[i + 1] = w >> 8;
+            }
+            c0setlc = 0;
+            ep0_send(0, 0, 0);
+          }
+          set_rx(0, ST_VALID);
+        }
+      } else if (n == 3) {
+        u16 cnt = BT_CRX(3) & 0x3FF, i, w;
+        for (i = 0; i < cnt; i += 2) {
+          w = PMA(EP3_RX + i);
+          ring_put(&rx, w);
+          if (i + 1 < cnt) ring_put(&rx, w >> 8);
+        }
+        rx_armed = 0;
+      }
+    }
+    if (v & 0x0080) {
+      clr_ctr_tx(n);
+      if (n == 0) {
+        if (c0addr_pend) { DADDR = 0x80 | c0addr; c0addr_pend = 0; }
+        ep0_next();
+      } else if (n == 2) tx_busy = 0;
+    }
+  }
+  pump();
+}
+
+int UsbCdc_Read(u8 *buf, int len)
+{
+  int i = 0;
+  NVIC_ICER0 = USB_LP_BIT;
+  usb_prio();
+  if ((CNTR & (CNTR_CTRM | CNTR_RESETM | 3)) != (CNTR_CTRM | CNTR_RESETM)) {
+    CNTR = CNTR_CTRM | CNTR_RESETM;
+    diag.fix++;
+  }
+  CNTR |= CNTR_SUSPM;
+  if (!configured) { NVIC_ISER0 = USB_LP_BIT; return 0; }
+  while (i < len && ring_cnt(&rx)) buf[i++] = ring_get(&rx);
+  pump();
+  NVIC_ISER0 = USB_LP_BIT;
+  return i;
+}
+
+int UsbCdc_Write(const u8 *buf, int len)
+{
+  int i = 0;
+  if (!configured) return 0;
+  NVIC_ICER0 = USB_LP_BIT;
+  while (i < len && ring_free(&tx)) ring_put(&tx, buf[i++]);
+  pump();
+  NVIC_ISER0 = USB_LP_BIT;
+  return i;
+}
+
+void UsbCdc_Init(void)
+{
+  vu32 d;
+
+  __USB_Init();
+
+  NVIC_ICER0 = USB_LP_BIT | USB_HP_BIT;
+  RCC_APB2ENR |= 0x4;                                  // GPIOA
+  RCC_APB1ENR |= 0x00800000;                           // USB
+  RCC_APB1RSTR |= 0x00800000;
+  RCC_APB1RSTR &= ~0x00800000UL;
+  RCC_APB1ENR &= ~0x00800000UL;
+
+  // Pull PA11/PA12 low for ~25 ms so the host sees a disconnect and re-enumerates us
+  GPIOA_CRH = (GPIOA_CRH & 0xFFF00FFF) | 0x00022000;
+  GPIOA_BRR = 0x1800;
+  for (d = 0; d < 400000; d++) { }
+  GPIOA_CRH = (GPIOA_CRH & 0xFFF00FFF) | 0x00044000;
+
+  RCC_APB1ENR |= 0x00800000;
+  CNTR = 0x01;                                         // FRES, powered up
+  for (d = 0; d < 1000; d++) { }
+  CNTR = 0;
+  ISTR = 0;
+  BTABLE = 0;
+  CNTR = CNTR_CTRM | CNTR_RESETM | CNTR_SUSPM;
+  usb_prio();
+  NVIC_ICPR0 = USB_LP_BIT | USB_HP_BIT;
+  NVIC_ISER0 = USB_LP_BIT;
+}
+
+const UsbDiag_t *UsbCdc_Diag(void)
+{
+  diag.cntr = CNTR;
+  diag.daddr = DADDR;
+  return &diag;
+}
+
+#endif
diff --git a/WildcatV6.5/UsbCmd.c b/WildcatV6.5/UsbCmd.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..23b3a95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/WildcatV6.5/UsbCmd.c
@@ -0,0 +1,346 @@
+#include "Interrupt.h"
+#include "Process.h"
+#include "Draw.h"
+#include "BIOS.h"
+#include "Menu.h"
+#include "UsbCmd.h"
+#include <string.h>
+
+#if USB_CDC
+
+#define CDC_VERSION   "6.5-cdc1"
+#define CAP_WAIT_T20  25          // 500 ms in 20 ms ticks
+#define TX_STALL_T20  50          // 1 s without the host draining anything
+
+vu8 UsbFrameCnt;
+
+extern u8  SelectiveUpdate;
+extern u16 XposRef;
+u16  GetXposRef(u16 XPos);
+u16  get_bag_max_buf(void);
+u8   OSBufferLogic(void);
+u8   ChartLogic(void);
+void ClearMeters(void);
+void ClearTrackBuff(u8 service);
+void ResetSum(void);
+void cleardatabuf(u8 service);
+void InitChart(void);
+void TriggFlagUpdate(void);
+
+static char line[64];
+static u8   ln, overflow;
+static u8   txb[64], txn, txfail;
+static u8   pend, cap_bps, cap_f0;
+static u32  cap_t0;
+
+// 20 ms ticks; Cnt_20mS wraps 50->0 as Sec_Cnt increments
+static u32 now20(void) { return (u32)Sec_Cnt * 51 + Cnt_20mS; }
+
+static void flush(void)
+{
+  u8 *p = txb;
+  int n = txn, k;
+  u32 t0 = now20();
+
+  txn = 0;
+  while (n > 0 && !txfail) {
+    k = UsbCdc_Write(p, n);
+    if (k > 0) { p += k; n -= k; t0 = now20(); }
+    else if (now20() - t0 > TX_STALL_T20) txfail = 1;
+  }
+}
+
+static void emit(u8 c)
+{
+  txb[txn++] = c;
+  if (txn == sizeof txb) flush();
+}
+
+static void ps(const char *s) { while (*s) emit(*s++); }
+
+static void pn(s32 v)
+{
+  char d[11];
+  u8 i = 0;
+  u32 u = v < 0 ? -(u32)v : (u32)v;
+
+  if (v < 0) emit('-');
+  do { d[i++] = '0' + u % 10; u /= 10; } while (u);
+  while (i) emit(d[--i]);
+}
+
+static void err(const char *why) { ps("ERR "); ps(why); emit('\n'); }
+static void ok(void)             { ps("OK\n"); }
+
+static u8 num(const char *s, s32 *out)
+{
+  s32 v = 0;
+  u8 neg = 0, digits = 0;
+
+  if (*s == '-') { neg = 1; s++; }
+  for (; *s >= '0' && *s <= '9'; s++) {
+    v = v * 10 + (*s - '0');
+    if (++digits > 6) return 0;
+  }
+  if (*s || !digits) return 0;
+  *out = neg ? -v : v;
+  return 1;
+}
+
+// excl = SelectiveUpdate bits for the Update_* calls this change does not need (0x02 range, 0x04 base, 0x10 trig)
+static void request_update(u8 excl)
+{
+  SelectiveUpdate |= excl | 0x08;     // 0x08: leave the signal generator alone
+  if (!Update) Update = 1;
+}
+
+static void send_cap(void)
+{
+  u16 n = get_bag_max_buf(), i;
+  u32 w;
+
+  ps("#CAP "); pn(n); emit(' '); pn(cap_bps); emit('\n');
+  for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+    w = DataBuf[i];
+    emit(w & 0xFF);
+    emit((w >> 8) & 0xFF);
+    if (cap_bps == 3) emit((w >> 16) & 3);
+  }
+  ps("\nOK\n");
+}
+
+static void cmd_ch(char **t)
+{
+  s32 v = 0;
+  u8 ch;
+  menu *m;
+
+  if (!strcmp(t[1], "A")) ch = TRACK1;
+  else if (!strcmp(t[1], "B")) ch = TRACK2;
+  else { err("channel"); return; }
+  m = Title[ch];
+
+  if (!strcmp(t[2], "RANGE")) {
+    if (!num(t[3], &v) || v < 0 || v > m[RANGE].Limit) { err("range"); return; }
+    m[RANGE].Value = v;
+    m[RANGE].Flag |= UPDAT;
+    SelectiveUpdate |= 0x20 << ch;
+  } else if (!strcmp(t[2], "OFFSET")) {
+    if (!num(t[3], &v) || v < 0 || v > m[POSI].Limit) { err("range"); return; }
+    m[POSI].Value = v;
+    m[POSI].Flag |= UPDAT;
+  } else if (!strcmp(t[2], "COUPLE")) {
+    if (!strcmp(t[3], "AC")) v = 1;
+    else if (strcmp(t[3], "DC")) { err("value"); return; }
+    m[COUPLE].Value = v;
+    m[COUPLE].Flag |= UPDAT;
+  } else { err("unknown"); return; }
+  request_update(0x04);
+  ok();
+}
+
+static void cmd_tb(char **t)
+{
+  s32 v;
+
+  if (!num(t[1], &v)) { err("value"); return; }
+  if (_Mode == SCAN || _Mode == X_Y) { err("mode"); return; }
+  if (v < 0 || v > Title[T_BASE][BASE].Limit) { err("range"); return; }
+
+  _T_base = v;
+  Title[T_BASE][BASE].Flag |= UPDAT;
+  if (FrameMode < 2) {
+    u16 x = GetXposRef(_X_posi.Value);
+    if (x > 150) XposRef = x;
+  }
+  // same as the menu: let Update_Base see a fresh untriggered state
+  if (!OSBufferLogic() && (__Get(FIFO_START) != 0 || (_Mode != NORH && _Mode != NORHLD)))
+    __Set(TRIGG_MODE, UNCONDITION);
+  if (_Mode == NORH || _Mode == NORHLD) { EnablePaS = 1; ResetSum(); }
+  request_update(0x02 | 0x10);
+  ok();
+}
+
+static void cmd_mode(char **t)
+{
+  s32 v;
+
+  if (!num(t[1], &v)) { err("value"); return; }
+  if (_Mode == SCAN || _Mode == X_Y || v < AUTO || v > SGL) { err("mode"); return; }
+  _Mode = v;
+  Title[T_BASE][MODE].Flag |= UPDAT;
+  request_update(0);
+  ok();
+}
+
+static void cmd_trig(char **t)
+{
+  s32 v;
+
+  if (Title[TRIGG][SOURCE].Value == 4) { err("ab mode"); return; }
+
+  if (!strcmp(t[1], "SRC")) {
+    if (t[2][0] < 'A' || t[2][0] > 'D' || t[2][1]) { err("value"); return; }
+    v = t[2][0] - 'A';
+    if (Title[v][SOURCE].Value == HIDE) { err("channel off"); return; }
+    Title[TRIGG][SOURCE].Value = v;
+  } else if (!strcmp(t[1], "KIND")) {
+    if (!num(t[2], &v) || v < 0 || v > Title[TRIGG][TR_KIND].Limit) { err("range"); return; }
+    _Tr_kind = v;
+  } else if (!strcmp(t[1], "LEVEL")) {
+    if (!num(t[2], &v) || v < 0 || v > Title[TRIGG][THRESHOLD].Limit) { err("range"); return; }
+    if (_Tr_source > 1) { err("source"); return; }
+    V_Trigg[_Tr_source].Value = v;
+  } else { err("unknown"); return; }
+  TriggFlagUpdate();
+  request_update(0x02 | 0x04);
+  ok();
+}
+
+static void cmd_run(void)
+{
+  if (_Status == RUN) { ok(); return; }
+  _State.Flag |= UPDAT;
+  _Status = RUN;
+  if (ChartLogic()) InitChart();
+  else {
+    SelectiveUpdate |= 0x60;
+    if (_Mode != NORH) ClearTrackBuff(1); else ClearLeadingEdge = 1;
+    __Set(FIFO_CLR, W_PTR);
+    cleardatabuf(2);
+    if (_T_base < 11) JumpCnt = 0;
+    EnablePaS = 1;
+    ResetSum();
+  }
+  ok();
+}
+
+static void cmd_state(void)
+{
+  ps("STATE RA="); pn(_A_Range);
+  ps(" RB=");      pn(_B_Range);
+  ps(" OA=");      pn(_1_posi);
+  ps(" OB=");      pn(_2_posi);
+  ps(" CA=");      pn(Title[TRACK1][COUPLE].Value);
+  ps(" CB=");      pn(Title[TRACK2][COUPLE].Value);
+  ps(" SA=");      pn(_1_source);
+  ps(" SB=");      pn(_2_source);
+  ps(" TB=");      pn(_T_base);
+  ps(" MODE=");    pn(_Mode);
+  ps(" TSRC=");    pn(_Tr_source);
+  ps(" TKIND=");   pn(_Tr_kind);
+  ps(" TLEVEL=");  pn(_Tr_source < 4 ? V_Trigg[_Tr_source].Value : 0);
+  ps(_Status == RUN ? " RUN=1" : " RUN=0");
+  ps(" N=");       pn(get_bag_max_buf());
+  ps(" AO=");      pn(ADCoffset);
+  emit('\n');
+}
+
+static void put_attr(const char *str)
+{
+  u8 i = 0, n = 0;
+
+  while (n < 8 && str[n]) n++;
+  while (n && str[n - 1] == ' ') n--;
+  while (i < n && str[i] == ' ') i++;
+  for (; i < n; i++) emit(str[i]);
+}
+
+static void cmd_tables(void)
+{
+  u16 i;
+
+  ps("TABLES V=");
+  for (i = 0; i <= G_Attr[0].Yp_Max; i++) { if (i) emit(','); put_attr(Y_Attr[i].STR); }
+  ps(" T=");
+  for (i = 0; i <= G_Attr[0].Xp_Max; i++) { if (i) emit(','); put_attr(X_Attr[i].STR); }
+  emit('\n');
+}
+
+static void cmd_diag(void)
+{
+  const UsbDiag_t *d = UsbCdc_Diag();
+
+  ps("DIAG ISR=");  pn(d->isr);
+  ps(" RST=");      pn(d->rst);
+  ps(" SUSP=");     pn(d->susp);
+  ps(" WKUP=");     pn(d->wkup);
+  ps(" ERR=");      pn(d->err);
+  ps(" FIX=");      pn(d->fix);
+  ps(" ISTR=");     pn(d->istr);
+  ps(" CNTR=");     pn(d->cntr);
+  ps(" ADDR=");     pn(d->daddr);
+  ps(" CFG=");      pn(d->cfg);
+  emit('\n');
+}
+
+static void cmd_cap(u8 bps)
+{
+  cap_bps = bps;
+  if (_Status != RUN) { send_cap(); return; }
+  cap_f0 = UsbFrameCnt;
+  cap_t0 = now20();
+  pend = 1;
+}
+
+static void execute(void)
+{
+  char *t[4];
+  u8 nt = 0, i;
+  char *p = line;
+
+  for (i = 0; line[i]; i++) if (line[i] >= 'a' && line[i] <= 'z') line[i] -= 32;
+  while (nt < 4) {
+    while (*p == ' ' || *p == '\t') p++;
+    if (!*p) break;
+    t[nt++] = p;
+    while (*p && *p != ' ' && *p != '\t') p++;
+    if (*p) *p++ = 0;
+  }
+  while (*p == ' ' || *p == '\t') p++;
+  if (*p) { err("args"); return; }
+  for (i = nt; i < 4; i++) t[i] = (char *)"";
+  if (!nt) return;
+
+  if (!strcmp(t[0], "*IDN?"))       { ps("DS203,Wildcat-CDC," CDC_VERSION "\n"); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "CH"))     { if (nt == 4) cmd_ch(t); else err("args"); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "TB"))     { if (nt == 2) cmd_tb(t); else err("args"); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "MODE"))   { if (nt == 2) cmd_mode(t); else err("args"); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "TRIG"))   { if (nt == 3) cmd_trig(t); else err("args"); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "RUN"))    cmd_run();
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "STOP"))   { ClearMeters(); _State.Flag |= UPDAT; _Status = HOLD; ok(); }
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "STATE?")) cmd_state();
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "TABLES?")) cmd_tables();
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "DIAG?"))  cmd_diag();
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "CAP?"))   cmd_cap(2);
+  else if (!strcmp(t[0], "CAPD?"))  cmd_cap(3);
+  else err("unknown");
+}
+
+void UsbCmd_Poll(void)
+{
+  u8 c;
+
+  if (pend) {
+    txfail = 0;
+    if (_Status != RUN || UsbFrameCnt != cap_f0) { pend = 0; send_cap(); }
+    else if (now20() - cap_t0 > CAP_WAIT_T20)    { pend = 0; err("timeout"); }
+    flush();
+    return;
+  }
+
+  while (!pend && UsbCdc_Read(&c, 1)) {
+    if (c == '\r') continue;
+    if (c != '\n') {
+      if (ln < sizeof line - 1) line[ln++] = c; else overflow = 1;
+      continue;
+    }
+    line[ln] = 0;
+    ln = 0;
+    txfail = 0;
+    if (overflow) { overflow = 0; err("overflow"); } else execute();
+    flush();
+  }
+}
+
+#endif
diff --git a/WildcatV6.5/build.sh b/WildcatV6.5/build.sh
new file mode 100755
